# Vendored provenance must round-trip byte-for-byte.
#
# The harness archive was verified byte-identical by recursive md5, and the
# rr-cache is content-addressed by conflict hash -- git normalising CRLF to LF in
# a preimage would silently stop the cache matching. The OSP config inputs are
# CRLF as shipped in 1999 and are an input to mkosp.py. So: no text conversion,
# no filtering, anywhere under vendor/.
vendor/** -text -diff
vendor/**/*.bundle binary

# The engine headers and game sources are vendored verbatim from q2pro
# and must stay byte-identical to the pin.
inc/** -text
src/** -text

# The shipped gamedir set.  `arena.cfg` is Rocket Arena 2's own
# arena-definition file -- 1028 lines, CRLF as it shipped.  The parser does not
# care, but a donor's file that git rewrites is no longer a copy of it.
#
# This rule stops GIT rewriting it; it cannot stop an EDITOR.  A whole-file
# rewrite that writes LF loses the property silently, because nothing checks and
# nothing breaks -- the parser's `fscanf("%s")` takes CR as whitespace.
# Restored to CRLF, and recorded so that "it is protected" is not read as
# "it cannot be lost".
colosseum/arena.cfg -text
